id: pm-gstv4k
title: "MCP agent identity and delegated authority: DPoP, workload identity federation, ID-JAG, and token exchange for agents acting alone or for users"
description: "Extend the issuer-bound 2026 authorization baseline into a standard identity and delegation model for autonomous workloads, user-on-behalf-of agents, and narrower sub-agent authority. Avoid pasted API keys and long-lived bearer credentials while preserving explainable consent and immutable provenance."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-identity,"area:mcp","area:security",delegation,dpop,token-exchange,workload-identity
created_at: "2026-08-28T20:22:23.663Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T20:58:32.013Z"
deadline: "2027-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 1200
acceptance_criteria: Agent and workload identities are cryptographically bound and discoverable without long-lived shared secrets; DPoP replay and nonce behavior follows current standards; workload federation ID-JAG and token exchange express user delegation and sub-agent attenuation; issuer audience scope actor and delegation chain are validated and recorded with privacy-safe provenance; revocation rotation expiry compromise and confused-deputy cases fail closed; SDK authorization policy is transport-neutral; threat models conformance fixtures real identity providers and adversarial tests gate release
parent: pm-opw1l3
risk: critical
confidence: medium
